# SABOTAGE: T78 (spec §I5) — `Samen.AI.Embeddings.embedder_simulated?/1` mirrors T152's
# `%Samen.AI.Completion{simulated:}` mechanism onto the embeddings/search lane (the
# retrieval primitive KB composer-suggestion + deflection both ride). This patch
# short-circuits `simulated_provider?/1` to a hardcoded `false`, so `Samen.AI.Embedder.
# Deterministic` — the ONLY embedder `:test` resolves to — never self-reports as
# simulated: the "SIMULATED ranking (keyless test embedder)" badge silently disappears
# from BOTH the composer-suggestion panel (TicketLive) and the portal deflection panel
# (PortalKbLive), presenting keyless hash-distance ranking as if it were a real semantic
# match — exactly the "never fabricate a suggestion as if real" guarantee the task hard
# rules require. A live provider's own (correctly-false) `simulated?/0` is unaffected —
# this sabotage only ever LIES in one direction (never claims a real provider is
# simulated; always claims a simulated one is real), the fail-honest inverse of the
# guarantee.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/embeddings_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the keyless :test-only deterministic fallback self-declares simulated
# MUST_FAIL: an explicit Deterministic override also reports simulated: true (provider self-declares, not env-gated)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/embeddings.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/embeddings.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/embeddings.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/embeddings.ex
@@ -186,10 +186,7 @@
   # real provider is simulated, never claim a keyless one is real). Wrapped so a provider whose
   # `simulated?/0` raises can never crash the caller.
   defp simulated_provider?(provider) do
-    Code.ensure_loaded?(provider) and function_exported?(provider, :simulated?, 0) and
-      provider.simulated?() == true
-  rescue
-    _ -> false
+    false
   end

